lmfback wrote:

> Come to think of it, with all the filtering going on in so many 
> softwares these days adding it to Nethack would not be too bad an idea.
> Let's say you could press CTRL F and the last message would never 
> appear again.
> The hard way to do this would be to dismiss that particular message 
> each time it appears but that would probably mean adding a lot of code 
> where the messages are generated (i.e. in several source files).
> The easy way would be to take that message, maybe analyze it a bit and 
> store the result in a buffer. For each message after that, check for a 
> match and possibly discard the new message. There's a possibility of 
> error here but it should be fairly easy to implement and most 
> errorenous discards are very likely CTRL F candidates anwyay.

What about allowing Regexp filters as an alternative? That should be 
fairly simple to implement, less prone to error and still very powerful.

